  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "process_ndpi_collected_info",
    "file": "ndpi/example/reader_util.c",
    "description": "In the TLS handling branch, the code calls strdup() on flow->ndpi_flow->protos.tls_quic_stun.tls_quic.issuerDN (and similar fields) after only checking for non-NULL pointer. It does not ensure the source is a valid NUL-terminated string. For this PoV, issuerDN points to invalid/non-terminated data, so strdup triggers strlen on a wild address and crashes.",
    "conditions": "Fuzz input is parsed as pcap and reaches packet_processing -> process_ndpi_collected_info for a flow classified as TLS/QUIC/TLS-master. The parser populates tls_quic fields with attacker-controlled pointer/content state where issuerDN is non-NULL but not a safe C string. When process_ndpi_collected_info executes `flow->ssh_tls.tls_issuerDN = strdup(...)`, ASan reports SEGV in strlen. Trigger requires reaching TLS metadata extraction with malformed certificate/handshake-derived string fields."
  },
